  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1003 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nFairly thick high cloud deck Monday night expected as an upper \nwave moves out of the Southern Rockies Monday night and eventually\ntracks across Texas through Tuesday. Clouds should keep overnight\nlows from totally bottoming out and have continued siding the \nforecast closer to traditional MOS versus the blended guidance \nnumbers. Most of the system's forcing remains confined to TX/LA \nand moisture is limited, thus a dry forecast is maintained for \nTuesday. Clouds plus continued influence from expansive Canadian \nhigh pressure will keep temps on the chilly side Tuesday, \ngenerally mid 40s north to lower 50s south.\n\nAFter a few nights of more widespread hard freezes this week, \nsouth winds will eventually return to the area under a dry \nnorthwest flow aloft. One impact will be more of a freeze-cured \nvegetative state to fine fuels, which quickly can become receptive\nto fire starts. Dry and warmer conditions will return but at \nleast no impactful fire weather appears on the horizon.",
